{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"449c8781c81b80560c48d438c5f04ae254ee1b517926c90172df054d3bb4a434","digest":{"component_or_area":"autodeploy timer and disk reclamation","key_entities":["infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","rebar-autodeploy.timer","rebar-root-disk-pressure","prune_docker_caches()","reclaim_under_pressure()","root_disk_pct()","DISK_PRESSURE_PCT","PRESSURE_PRUNE_MIN_INTERVAL","PRESSURE_PRUNE_TS_FILE","BUILD_CACHE_KEEP","AUTODEPLOY_DISK_PRESSURE","STATE_DIR","/etc/rebar/autodeploy.env","tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py"],"problem_keywords":["disk pressure","docker prune","no-op tick","root filesystem","throttle","autodeploy","garbage collection"],"propositions":["autodeploy.sh's no-op early exit (line 228) does not invoke prune_docker_caches(), leaving garbage unclaimed between deploys when main is quiescent","root disk fills to 92–96% during build bursts because pressure-triggered reclaim only runs on deploy and backoff paths, not the ~2-min no-op ticks","prune_docker_caches() is defined after line 228, making it uncallable from the no-op exit without relocation","adding pressure-triggered prune to the no-op path requires relocating prune_docker_caches() from ~line 245 into the helper block near line 150 so it precedes the new call site","a throttled reclaim on each no-op tick, triggered when root disk usage >= 80% and the last prune was >600s ago, will reclaim garbage without churn during quiescent periods"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787901274561978001,"uuid":"8c6c4f32-207d-4c82-b4df-ad0db8f27023"}